    "chapterId": 74,
    "fileId": 6204,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Cutaneous angiosarcoma</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>The dermis contains ill-defined tumour composed of irregular vascular channels lined by hyperchromatic, moderately atypical vascular endothelial cells. There is a marked surrounding chronic inflammatory infiltrate that makes the tumour difficult to discern.</p>",
    "source": "Steven D. Billings",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/33/74/6204.jpg",
